      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KINGS GALLERY (10) returned from a break in very good order last time out when a commanding winner over 2240m at Melton on August 12, getting home by 6 metres. Will need an ounce of luck to slot in from this tricky draw so things might not go so smoothly but he was so impressive there off the telling trial that he simply must be seen as the one they have to take down. BLUE MIKI (7) finished second last start over 1690m at this track, beaten 2.75 metres. That was an improvement on the unplaced effort at Maryborough the run before. Leading hope if things go his way. TOOBY GOLD (6) is the next best after finishing runner-up over 1720m at Melton last time out. HIGHVIEW HAMMER (5) disappointed last time when tenth over 1609m at Cranbourne but can do a lot better so worth considering.",
